{"title":"1996 OIM Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_OIM_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Three pieces <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are located one at each vertex of an equilateral triangle of side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. The triangle has been divided into equilateral triangles with side 1, as shown in the figure for the case when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/3/5635737307f5f0651cced8ee2e6558a426fd27b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=3$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p>\n<figure class=\"mw-default-size mw-halign-center\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Ibe11_2.gif\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/6/60/Ibe11_2.gif\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"163\" height=\"139\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>Initially all the lines of the figure are painted blue. The pieces move along the lines, painting their path red, according to the following two rules:\n</p><p>i. First, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> moves, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and so on in turns. On each turn each checker travels exactly one side of a triangle from one end to the other.\n</p><p>ii. No piece can travel along one side of a triangle that is already painted red; but it can rest on a painted end, even if there is already another piece waiting there for its turn.\n</p><p>Show that for all integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/4/0247db3d702b5ce6be98f50771750a2723cddcea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" /> it is possible to paint all the sides of the triangles red.\n</p><p>~translated into English by Tomas Diaz. ~orders@tomasdiaz.com\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_OIM_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><i>This problem needs a solution. If you have a solution for it, please help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1996_OIM_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit\">adding it</a></span>.</i> \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_OIM_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.oma.org.ar/enunciados/ibe11.htm\">https://www.oma.org.ar/enunciados/ibe11.htm</a>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017190014\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.025 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.086 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 67/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 423/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 1688/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.627      1 Template:Solution\n100.00%    5.627      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:26105:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017190014 and revision id 207087. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}